          "reasoning": "On app-01 the 'ubuntu' user, working in an interactive login shell (-bash, pid 5677), ran 'useradd jsmith' without sudo at 12:23:05. That attempt ran as ubuntu and could not succeed. Four seconds later the same user ran 'sudo useradd jsmith', which started useradd as root (the trigger process). useradd then started its normal PAM helper, 'pam_tally2 --user jsmith --reset --quiet'. sudo's only network activity was a DNS lookup to the local systemd-resolved stub (127.0.0.53:53), which sudo normally does. At 12:23:26 the same shell ran 'sudo adduser svc_backup'. A failed attempt followed by a sudo retry from a human shell, standard system binaries, nothing downloaded and no outside connections all fit an admin creating accounts by hand, not an attack. I did not look at what the second adduser run did. Suggested follow-up: confirm with the app-01 admin that jsmith and svc_backup were approved accounts.",
